      "content": "That's a pretty big gap in the scores. I'm trying to understand if it's just the specific words or if it's more about the underlying competence. \n\nIf I took Snippet B and just swapped the slang for slightly more formal words, but kept the same grammar structure—like, \"We need to ensure we fix how we are doing things if we want to see profit go up\"—would the score change much? Or is there something about the way the speaker actually constructs the ideas that makes them seem less capable of leading a company?",
